<!DOCTYPE qhelp SYSTEM "qhelp.dtd">
<qhelp>
    <overview>
        <p>
            Desktop URL handlers accept every scheme registered with the operating system.
            Passing an untrusted URL to one of these handlers can invoke an unintended
            application or expose local resources.
        </p>
    </overview>
    <recommendation>
        <p>
            Parse the URL and allow only the schemes required by the application before
            invoking the protocol handler. For web links, allow only HTTP and HTTPS.
        </p>
    </recommendation>
    <example>
        <sample src="PotentiallyUnguardedProtocolHandler.cpp" />
        <p>
            The bad example opens an untrusted URL directly. The good example first
            checks that the URL uses HTTPS.
        </p>
    </example>
    <references>
        <li>
            CVE-2022-43550: <a href="https://hackerone.com/reports/1692603">Jitsi Desktop
            Client RCE by interacting with malicious URL schemes</a>
        </li>
    </references>
</qhelp>
